[149.926503, "o", "   740\tRisk assessment WP-5948 ties intercompany netting dispute to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   741\t\r\n   742\tInterview #991 with corporate accounting highlighted how intercompany netting dispute statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n   743\t\r\n   744\tLead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that intercompany netting dispute created reconciliation noise in corporate accounting during April settlement. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   745\t\r\n   746\tSite visit #512 to corporate accounting captured mailbox exports showing how intercompany netting dispute correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  "]
[149.926708, "o", " 747\t\r\n   748\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   749\t\r\n   750\tThe committee packet references intercompany netting dispute as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   751\t\r\n   752\tLead reviewer R. Okonkwo noted that intercompany netting dispute created reconciliation noise in corporate accounting during April settlement. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   753\t\r\n   754\t## Case Study 07 — Capital Project Capitalization\r\n   755\t\r\n   756\tFollow-up #812 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical le"]
[149.926726, "o", "dger and structured sections at file end.\r\n   757\t\r\n   758\tFollow-up #906 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n   759\t\r\n   760\tDuring July review, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   761\t\r\n   762\tWorking paper WP-1990 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   763\t\r\n   764\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   765\t\r\n   766"]
[149.926901, "o", "\tDuring July review, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n"]
