[336.461597, "o", "   940\tWorking paper WP-2874 documents a three-way match failure tied to lease modification restatement. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   941\t\r\n   942\tDuring August memo, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on lease modification restatement. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   943\t\r\n   944\tDuring August memo, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on lease modification restatement. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   945\t\r\n   946\tThe committee packet references lease modification restatement as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   947\t\r\n   948\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compar"]
[336.462036, "o", "ed compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   949\t\r\n   950\tIn August memo, external advisors reviewed lease modification restatement and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   951\t\r\n   952\tIn August memo, external advisors reviewed lease modification restatement and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   953\t\r\n   954\tWorking paper WP-6452 documents a three-way match failure tied to lease modification restatement. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   955\t\r\n   956\tDuring August memo, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on lease modification restatement. Finance opera"]
[336.462133, "o", "tions pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   957\t\r\n   958\tRisk assessment WP-5172 ties lease modification restatement to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   959\t\r\n   960\tInterview #613 with technical accounting highlighted how lease modification restatement statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n   961\t\r\n   962\tIn August memo, external advisors reviewed lease modification restatement and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   963\t\r\n   964\tLead reviewer J. Huang noted that lease modification restatement created reconciliation noise in technical accounting during Aug"]
[336.462317, "o", "ust memo. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   965\t\r\n   966\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   967\t\r\n   968\tMemo WP-5231 summarizes stakeholder interviews about lease modification restatement. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   969\t\r\n   970\t## Policy Exceptions (draft)\r\n   971\t\r\n   972\tDraft waiver log — not authoritative for extract output.\r\n   973\t\r\n   974\t### Policy Exception\r\n   975\ttransaction: TXN-de3b42d7-919c-5839-a490-b039d9c97092\r\n   976\tapproved_by: compliance\r\n   977\treason: draft waiver (superseded)\r\n   978\t\r\n   979\t### Policy Exception\r\n   980\ttransaction: TXN-68b5423c-1abb-59e6-947e-7e56011cec58\r\n   981\tapproved"]
[336.463022, "o", "_by: finance\r\n   982\treason: draft waiver (superseded)\r\n   983\t\r\n   984\t## Case Study 09 — Revenue Cutoff Testing\r\n   985\t\r\n   986\tDuring September fieldwork, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on revenue cutoff testing. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   987\t\r\n   988\tWorking paper WP-9812 documents a three-way match failure tied to revenue cutoff testing. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   989\t\r\n   990\tIn September fieldwork, external advisors reviewed revenue cutoff testing and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   991\t\r\n   992\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amen"]
[336.463115, "o", "dment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   993\t\r\n   994\tSite visit #110 to external audit captured mailbox exports showing how revenue cutoff testing correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n   995\t\r\n   996\tIn September fieldwork, external advisors reviewed revenue cutoff testing and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   997\t\r\n   998\tLead reviewer A. Ndiaye noted that revenue cutoff testing created reconciliation noise in external audit during September fieldwork. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   999\t\r\n  1000\tThe committee packet references revenue cutoff testing as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes b"]
