[336.464266, "o", "g to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1053\t\r\n  1054\tSite visit #937 to external audit captured mailbox exports showing how revenue cutoff testing correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1055\t\r\n  1056\tLead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that revenue cutoff testing created reconciliation noise in external audit during September fieldwork. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1057\t\r\n  1058\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n  1059\t\r\n  1060\tAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n  1061\t\r\n  1062\tAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n  1063\tledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n  1064\tsets field `date` or `status`, u"]
[336.465887, "o", "se that notice's `effective` date as\r\n  1065\t`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n  1066\tkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n  1067\tplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n  1068\t\r\n  1069\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output — field notes\r\n  1070\t\r\n  1071\tFollow-up #977 confirmed that external audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for revenue cutoff testing. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1072\t\r\n  1073\tMemo WP-3912 summarizes stakeholder interviews about revenue cutoff testing. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1074\t\r\n  1075\tFollow-up #283 confirmed that external audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for revenue cutoff testing. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger"]
