[338.533043, "o", "  1425\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n  1426\tfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n  1427\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n  1428\t\r\n  1429\t`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n  1430\tby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n  1431\t(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n  1432\tsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n  1433\ttransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n  1434\tsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n  1435\t`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n  1436\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n  1437\tnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n  1438\tby notice_id ascending.\r\n  1439\t\r\n  1440\t## Investigation Brief 08 —"]
[338.533503, "o", " Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts — field notes\r\n  1441\t\r\n  1442\tDuring July review, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1443\t\r\n  1444\tRisk assessment WP-5486 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1445\t\r\n  1446\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1447\t\r\n  1448\tMemo WP-5276 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  144"]
