[384.734868, "o", " transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1821\t\r\n  1822\tMemo WP-4038 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1823\t\r\n  1824\tWorking paper WP-6587 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1825\t\r\n  1826\tThe committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1827\t\r\n  1828\tMemo WP-9951 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor"]
