[386.680343, "o", "ractor.\r\n  1300\t\r\n  1301\tSite visit #700 to compliance captured mailbox exports showing how grant compliance attestation correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1302\t\r\n  1303\tIn November certification, external advisors reviewed grant compliance attestation and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1304\t\r\n  1305\tThe committee packet references grant compliance attestation as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1306\t\r\n  1307\tMemo WP-4583 summarizes stakeholder interviews about grant compliance attestation. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1308\t\r\n  1309\tDuri"]
[386.680368, "o", "ng November certification, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on grant compliance attestation. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1310\t\r\n  1311\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1312\t\r\n  1313\tThe committee packet references grant compliance attestation as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1314\t\r\n  1315\tWorking paper WP-5560 documents a three-way match failure tied to grant compliance attestation. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1316\t\r\n  1317\tFollow-up #468 confirmed that compliance had been using an informal spread"]
[386.680393, "o", "sheet for grant compliance attestation. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1318\t\r\n  1319\tFollow-up #201 confirmed that compliance had been using an informal spreadsheet for grant compliance attestation. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1320\t\r\n  1321\tInterview #490 with compliance highlighted how grant compliance attestation statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1322\t\r\n  1323\tInterview #237 with compliance highlighted how grant compliance attestation statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1324\t\r\n  1325\tWorking paper WP-7086 documents a three-way match failure tied to grant compliance attesta"]
[386.68042, "o", "tion. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1326\t\r\n  1327\tRisk assessment WP-2238 ties grant compliance attestation to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1328\t\r\n  1329\tFollow-up #732 confirmed that compliance had been using an informal spreadsheet for grant compliance attestation. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1330\t\r\n  1331\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1332\t\r\n"]
[386.680445, "o", "  1333\tRisk assessment WP-9724 ties grant compliance attestation to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1334\t\r\n  1335\tSite visit #353 to compliance captured mailbox exports showing how grant compliance attestation correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1336\t\r\n  1337\tIn November certification, external advisors reviewed grant compliance attestation and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1338\t\r\n"]
[386.68047, "o", "  1339\tInterview #844 with compliance highlighted how grant compliance attestation statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1340\t\r\n  1341\tMemo WP-7589 summarizes stakeholder interviews about grant compliance attestation. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1342\t\r\n  1343\tMemo WP-2412 summarizes stakeholder interviews about grant compliance attestation. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n"]
[386.680495, "o", "  1344\t\r\n  1345\t## Case Study 12 — Year-End Close Checklist Drift\r\n  1346\t\r\n  1347\tFollow-up #464 confirmed that controller had been using an informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1348\t\r\n"]
[386.680522, "o", "  1349\tDuring December freeze, L. Bergstrom circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1350\t\r\n  1351\tMemo WP-4599 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1352\t\r\n  1353\tDuring December freeze, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n"]
[386.680546, "o", "  1354\t\r\n  1355\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1356\t\r\n  1357\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1358\t\r\n  1359\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n"]
[386.680583, "o", "  1360\t\r\n  1361\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1362\t\r\n  1363\tRisk assessment WP-3264 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1364\t\r\n"]
[386.680611, "o", "  1365\tMemo WP-4783 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1366\t\r\n  1367\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1368\t\r\n  1369\tDuring December freeze, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1370\t\r\n  1371\tMemo WP-2571 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1372\t\r\n"]
