[404.781905, "o", "informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1348\t\r\n  1349\tDuring December freeze, L. Bergstrom circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1350\t\r\n  1351\tMemo WP-4599 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1352\t\r\n  1353\tDuring December freeze, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1354\t\r\n  1355\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a mac"]
[404.781926, "o", "hine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1356\t\r\n  1357\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1358\t\r\n  1359\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1360\t\r\n  1361\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1362\t\r\n  1363\tRisk assessment WP-3264 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not tre"]
[404.781938, "o", "at decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1364\t\r\n  1365\tMemo WP-4783 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1366\t\r\n  1367\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1368\t\r\n  1369\tDuring December freeze, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1370\t\r\n  1371\tMemo WP-2571 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 r"]
[404.78195, "o", "esolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1372\t\r\n  1373\tMemo WP-1476 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1374\t\r\n  1375\tFollow-up #830 confirmed that controller had been using an informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1376\t\r\n  1377\tDuring December freeze, J. Huang circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1378\t\r\n  1379\tInterview #272 with controller highlighted how year-end close checklist drift statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail"]
[404.781961, "o", " timestamps.\r\n  1380\t\r\n  1381\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1382\t\r\n  1383\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1384\t\r\n  1385\tRisk assessment WP-4040 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1386\t\r\n  1387\tSite visit #697 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1388\t\r\n  1389\tIn December freeze, external "]
[404.781972, "o", "advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1390\t\r\n  1391\tFollow-up #385 confirmed that controller had been using an informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1392\t\r\n  1393\tLead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1394\t\r\n  1395\tMemo WP-7089 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1396\t\r\n  1397\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is"]
[404.781981, "o", " non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1398\t\r\n  1399\tRisk assessment WP-5420 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1400\t\r\n  1401\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1402\t\r\n  1403\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1404\t\r\n  1405\tWorking paper WP-2580 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-"]
[404.781991, "o", "end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1406\t\r\n  1407\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1408\t\r\n  1409\tWorking paper WP-4368 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1410\t\r\n  1411\tWorking paper WP-8280 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1412\t\r\n  1413\tLead reviewer S. Patel noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blame"]
[404.781999, "o", "d tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1414\t\r\n  1415\tWorking paper WP-3865 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1416\t\r\n  1417\tSite visit #634 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1418\t\r\n  1419\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n  1420\t\r\n  1421\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n  1422\t\r\n  1423\tContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n  1424\t`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n  1425\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n  1426\tfinal status is `reversed`"]
[404.782009, "o", ", `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n  1427\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n  1428\t\r\n  1429\t`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n  1430\tby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n  1431\t(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n  1432\tsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n  1433\ttransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n  1434\tsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n  1435\t`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n  1436\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n  1437\tnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n  1438\tby notice_id ascending.\r\n  1439\t\r\n  1440\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts — field notes\r\n  1441\t\r\n"]
[404.789035, "o", "  1213\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I) — field notes\r\n  1214\t\r\n"]
[404.78929, "o", "  1215\tMemo WP-7758 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1216\t\r\n  1217\tIn Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1218\t\r\n  1219\tDuring Q1 close, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1220\t\r\n  1221\tRisk assessment WP-8021 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n"]
[404.789328, "o", "  1222\t\r\n  1223\tWorking paper WP-3669 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1224\t\r\n  1225\tSite visit #351 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1226\t\r\n  1227\tMemo WP-1992 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1228\t\r\n  1229\tThe committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1230\t\r\n  1231\tLead reviewer J. Huang noted that vendor onboarding backlog created r"]
