[447.481497, "o", "  1201\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n  1202\t\r\n  1203\tExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n  1204\t\r\n  1205\tException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n  1206\t`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n  1207\twhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n  1208\tthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n  1209\tcomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n  1210\t(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n  1211\tlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n  1212\t\r\n  1213\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I) — field notes\r\n  1214\t\r\n  1215\tMemo WP-7758 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1216\t\r\n  1217\tIn Q1 cl"]
[447.481527, "o", "ose, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1218\t\r\n  1219\tDuring Q1 close, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1220\t\r\n  1221\tRisk assessment WP-8021 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1222\t\r\n  1223\tWorking paper WP-3669 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1224\t\r\n  1225\tSite visit #351 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspo"]
[447.481535, "o", "ndence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1226\t\r\n  1227\tMemo WP-1992 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1228\t\r\n  1229\tThe committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1230\t\r\n  1231\tLead reviewer J. Huang noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1232\t\r\n  1233\tFollow-up #132 confirmed that procurement had been using an informal spreadsheet for vendor onboarding backlog. The formal extractor must instead derive rows o"]
[447.481544, "o", "nly from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1234\t\r\n  1235\tThe committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1236\t\r\n  1237\tRisk assessment WP-8866 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1238\t\r\n  1239\tDuring Q1 close, M. Chen circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1240\t\r\n  1241\tIn Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1242\t\r\n  1243\tSit"]
[447.482266, "o", "e visit #637 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1244\t\r\n  1245\tWorking paper WP-6845 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1246\t\r\n  1247\tFollow-up #252 confirmed that procurement had been using an informal spreadsheet for vendor onboarding backlog. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1248\t\r\n  1249\tRisk assessment WP-4815 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1250\t\r\n  1251\tThe committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to lat"]
[447.482278, "o", "e compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1252\t\r\n  1253\tInterview #952 with procurement highlighted how vendor onboarding backlog statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1254\t\r\n  1255\tInterview #820 with procurement highlighted how vendor onboarding backlog statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1256\t\r\n  1257\tWorking paper WP-3660 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1258\t\r\n  1259\tIn Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrat"]
[447.482286, "o", "ive context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1260\t\r\n  1261\tDuring Q1 close, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1262\t\r\n  1263\tSite visit #394 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1264\t\r\n  1265\tWorking paper WP-6026 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1266\t\r\n  1267\tWorking paper WP-8575 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1268\t\r\n "]
[447.482293, "o", " 1269\tFollow-up #489 confirmed that procurement had been using an informal spreadsheet for vendor onboarding backlog. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1270\t\r\n  1271\t## Case Study 11 — Grant Compliance Attestation\r\n  1272\t\r\n  1273\tRisk assessment WP-9565 ties grant compliance attestation to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1274\t\r\n  1275\tMemo WP-2248 summarizes stakeholder interviews about grant compliance attestation. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1276\t\r\n  1277\tFollow-up #885 confirmed that compliance had been using an informal spreadsheet for grant compliance attestation. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1278\t\r\n  "]
[447.484396, "o", "1279\tDuring November certification, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on grant compliance attestation. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1280\t\r\n  1281\tThe committee packet references grant compliance attestation as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1282\t\r\n  1283\tFollow-up #748 confirmed that compliance had been using an informal spreadsheet for grant compliance attestation. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n  1284\t\r\n  1285\tInterview #393 with compliance highlighted how grant compliance attestation statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  1286\t\r\n  1287\tDraft guidance in this paragraph "]
[447.484687, "o", "is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1288\t\r\n  1289\tLead reviewer J. Huang noted that grant compliance attestation created reconciliation noise in compliance during November certification. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1290\t\r\n  1291\tMemo WP-4066 summarizes stakeholder interviews about grant compliance attestation. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1292\t\r\n  1293\tIn November certification, external advisors reviewed grant compliance attestation and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1294\t\r\n  1295\tMemo WP-4789 summarizes stakeholde"]
