[447.485892, "o", "iliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1414\t\r\n  1415\tWorking paper WP-3865 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n  1416\t\r\n  1417\tSite visit #634 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n  1418\t\r\n  1419\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n  1420\t\r\n  1421\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n  1422\t\r\n  1423\tContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n  1424\t`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n  1425\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its "]
[447.485911, "o", "own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n  1426\tfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n  1427\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n  1428\t\r\n  1429\t`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n  1430\tby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n  1431\t(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n  1432\tsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n  1433\ttransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n  1434\tsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n  1435\t`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n  1436\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n  1437\tnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n  1438\tby notice_id ascending.\r\n  1439\t\r\n  1440\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts — "]
[447.485922, "o", "field notes\r\n  1441\t\r\n  1442\tDuring July review, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  1443\t\r\n  1444\tRisk assessment WP-5486 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1445\t\r\n  1446\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n  1447\t\r\n  1448\tMemo WP-5276 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1449\t\r\n  1450\tLead reviewer M. Chen noted that c"]
[447.486001, "o", "apital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n  1451\t\r\n  1452\tThe committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n  1453\t\r\n  1454\tFollow-up #632 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end."]
[447.486711, "o", "\r\n  1455\t\r\n  1456\tIn July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n  1457\t\r\n  1458\tMemo WP-6380 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n  1459\t\r\n  1460\tRisk assessment WP-3664 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n  1461\t\r\n"]
