[449.89791, "o", "   220\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   221\t\r\n   222\tRisk assessment WP-2046 ties treasury wire cutoff failures to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   223\t\r\n   224\tThe committee packet references treasury wire cutoff failures as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   225\t\r\n   226\tMemo WP-9086 summarizes stakeholder interviews about treasury wire cutoff failures. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   227\t\r\n   228\tFollow-up #736 confirmed that treasury had been using an informal s"]
[449.897943, "o", "preadsheet for treasury wire cutoff failures. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n   229\t\r\n   230\tThe committee packet references treasury wire cutoff failures as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   231\t\r\n   232\tThe committee packet references treasury wire cutoff failures as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   233\t\r\n   234\tMemo WP-9556 summarizes stakeholder interviews about treasury wire cutoff failures. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   235\t\r\n   236\tWorking paper WP-6752 documents a three-way match failure tied to treasury wire cutoff failures. The team escalated when repeated extractor"]
[449.89795, "o", " runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   237\t\r\n   238\t## Email Excerpts (archived thread)\r\n   239\t\r\n   240\tNon-authoritative mailbox export kept for chronology; do not merge these rows.\r\n   241\t\r\n   242\tFrom: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   243\tSubject: Re: TXN-88519dfd-79ff-5de0-ae59-862ab932bc25\r\n   244\tsent: 2020-01-01\r\n   245\tstatus: reversed\r\n   246\t\r\n   247\tFrom: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   248\tSubject: Re: TXN-51cc9d8a-ea13-56ab-af16-c55e1716132f\r\n   249\tsent: 2024-01-01\r\n   250\tstatus: approved\r\n   251\t\r\n   252\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n   253\t\r\n   254\tAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n   255\t\r\n   256\tInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   257\tamendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   258\toutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   259\trejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   260\tcont"]
[449.897973, "o", "ains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n   261\t\r\n   262\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence — field notes\r\n   263\t\r\n   264\tRisk assessment WP-2138 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   265\t\r\n   266\tWorking paper WP-3210 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   267\t\r\n   268\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   269\t\r\n   270\tWorking paper WP-6073 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produce"]
[449.899904, "o", "d different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   271\t\r\n   272\tLead reviewer J. Huang noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   273\t\r\n   274\tThe committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   275\t\r\n   276\tLead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   277\t\r\n   278\tFollow-up #238 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger an"]
[449.899942, "o", "d structured sections at file end.\r\n   279\t\r\n   280\tWorking paper WP-3893 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   281\t\r\n   282\tIn July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   283\t\r\n   284\tMemo WP-2881 summarizes stakeholder interviews about capital project capitalization. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   285\t\r\n   286\tDuring July review, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   287\t\r\n   288\tIn"]
[449.899951, "o", "terview #586 with fixed assets highlighted how capital project capitalization statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n   289\t\r\n   290\tRisk assessment WP-4038 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   291\t\r\n   292\tWorking paper WP-2952 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   293\t\r\n   294\tThe committee packet references capital project capitalization as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   295\t\r\n   296\tIn July review, external advisors reviewed capital project capitalization a"]
