[512.746284, "o", "   468\t## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n   469\t\r\n   470\tExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n   471\t\r\n   472\tThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n   473\tmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n   474\t`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n   475\tequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n   476\tapply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n   477\tafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n   478\t\r\n   479\t## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — field notes\r\n   480\t\r\n   481\tLead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   482\t\r\n   483\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-bin"]
[512.746451, "o", "ding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n   484\t\r\n   485\tMemo WP-3037 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   486\t\r\n   487\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   488\t\r\n   489\tWorking paper WP-7415 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   490\t\r\n   491\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing facto"]
[512.748072, "o", "r to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   492\t\r\n   493\tSite visit #268 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n   494\t\r\n   495\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   496\t\r\n   497\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   498\t\r\n   499\tRisk assessment WP-3524 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around ma"]
[512.748256, "o", "il ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   500\t\r\n   501\tMemo WP-3030 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   502\t\r\n   503\tWorking paper WP-4438 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   504\t\r\n   505\tMemo WP-1550 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   506\t\r\n   507\tDuring December freeze, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA "]
[512.74828, "o", "reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   508\t\r\n   509\tIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n   510\t\r\n   511\tDuring December freeze, L. Bergstrom circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n   512\t\r\n   513\tFollow-up #968 confirmed that controller had been using an informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n   514\t\r\n   515\tSite visit #159 to controller captured mailbox exports showing how year-end close checklist drift correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effecti"]
[512.7483, "o", "ve-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n   516\t\r\n   517\tLead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n   518\t\r\n   519\tInterview #849 with controller highlighted how year-end close checklist drift statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n   520\t\r\n   521\tRisk assessment WP-7640 ties year-end close checklist drift to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   522\t\r\n   523\tWorking paper WP-2453 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   52"]
