[518.766675, "o", "   232\tThe committee packet references treasury wire cutoff failures as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n   233\t\r\n   234\tMemo WP-9556 summarizes stakeholder interviews about treasury wire cutoff failures. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n   235\t\r\n   236\tWorking paper WP-6752 documents a three-way match failure tied to treasury wire cutoff failures. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n   237\t\r\n   238\t## Email Excerpts (archived thread)\r\n   239\t\r\n   240\tNon-authoritative mailbox export kept for chronology; do not merge these rows.\r\n   241\t\r\n   242\tFrom: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   243\tSubject: Re: TXN-88519dfd-79ff-5de0-ae59-862ab932bc25\r\n   244\tsent: 2020-01-01\r\n   245\tstatus: reversed\r\n   246\t\r\n   247\tFrom: co"]
[518.766712, "o", "mpliance@corp.internal\r\n   248\tSubject: Re: TXN-51cc9d8a-ea13-56ab-af16-c55e1716132f\r\n   249\tsent: 2024-01-01\r\n   250\tstatus: approved\r\n   251\t\r\n   252\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n   253\t\r\n   254\tAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n   255\t\r\n   256\tInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   257\tamendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   258\toutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   259\trejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   260\tcontains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n   261\t\r\n   262\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence — field notes\r\n   263\t\r\n   264\tRisk assessment WP-2138 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n   265\t\r\n   266\tWorking"]
[518.766724, "o", " paper WP-3210 documents a three-way match failure tied to capital project capitalization. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n"]
