[579.213976, "o", "## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n"]
[579.214016, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214053, "o", "Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n"]
[579.214071, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214089, "o", "Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n"]
[579.214107, "o", "amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n"]
[579.214125, "o", "only, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n"]
[579.214144, "o", "ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n"]
[579.214161, "o", "in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n"]
[579.214179, "o", "before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n"]
[579.214196, "o", "mail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n"]
[579.214214, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214231, "o", "## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment — field notes\r\n"]
[579.214248, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214267, "o", "During July review, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on capital project capitalization. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n"]
[579.214285, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214303, "o", "Lead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n"]
[579.21432, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214338, "o", "Risk assessment WP-7766 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n"]
[579.214355, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214374, "o", "Follow-up #977 confirmed that fixed assets had been using an informal spreadsheet for capital project capitalization. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n"]
[579.214391, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214409, "o", "Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n"]
[579.214426, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214444, "o", "Site visit #872 to fixed assets captured mailbox exports showing how capital project capitalization correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n"]
[579.214462, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.21448, "o", "Risk assessment WP-9137 ties capital project capitalization to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n"]
[579.2145, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214529, "o", "Lead reviewer A. Ndiaye noted that capital project capitalization created reconciliation noise in fixed assets during July review. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n"]
[579.214558, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214597, "o", "Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n"]
[579.214625, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214657, "o", "Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n"]
[579.214682, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214701, "o", "Interview #628 with fixed assets highlighted how capital project capitalization statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n"]
[579.214718, "o", "\r\n"]
[579.214737, "o", "Site visit #975 to fixed assets captured mailbox exports showing how capital project capitalization correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n"]
